WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.740
Follow heat beyond the coupling.

2
00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:06.060
Equipment transfers heat to coolant, the rack routes it through its manifold

3
00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:09.380
and connections, and the receiving system must carry it to an adequate

4
00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:10.460
heat-rejection path.

5
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.980
A coolant distribution unit, or C D U, may separate the technology

6
00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:17.100
cooling system from the facility water system.

7
00:00:17.621 --> 00:00:21.560
The technology cooling system, often called T C S, serves the equipment

8
00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:22.580
side of that boundary.

9
00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.920
The facility water system, or F W S, serves the receiving side

10
00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.080
in the illustrated arrangement.

11
00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:33.240
These terms locate responsibilities; they do not imply identical fluid chemistry or

12
00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:35.040
operating conditions on both sides.

13
00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:38.020
Keep the residual air-side heat visible.

14
00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:42.380
A liquid path that meets its own requirement can coexist with insufficient

15
00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:43.760
airflow for other components.

16
00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:45.700
The system review needs both.

17
00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:50.960
Define where temperatures, flows and pressures are guaranteed, and which party demonstrates

18
00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:53.340
heat rejection under the agreed operating cases.

19
00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:57.480
The linked C D U course provides specialist depth without replacing the

20
00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:59.160
configured-rack acceptance evidence.

